rows.en:
He wasn't allowed back in the exam room until that exam was over, so he had to be waiting somewhere.
He wasn't anywhere near the restroom.
Well, nobody would hang around a creepy place like that forever.{p}

I worked up my courage and decided to go into the restroom.
As I approached, the hands began writhing violently, trying to grab me.
Even so, everyone else passed right through the hands and went in as if nothing were there.{p}

Apparently, in that restroom, hands come out of the toilet.
And if the hands take a liking to you, you get taken away to the spirit world.
Of course, they only come out of the toilet bowl; there don't seem to be any rumors of anyone seeing hands filling the whole doorway like I did back then.{p}

I opened the heavy door, and there was the roof.
They wouldn't be able to follow me this far.
I caught my breath and looked back at the stairs.{p}

I swung my leg over the fence and looked down at the ground.
If I got down there, I could escape.
I closed my eyes and jumped.{p}

"Let's get out of here☆"
We broke into a run together.
Behind us, I could sense something rustling.{p}

While they did, we dashed out into the schoolyard.
Under the weak sunlight, the schoolyard felt so peaceful that everything up to then seemed like a bad dream.
We looked at each other, and then up at the school building.{p}

"Abandoned" makes it sound so bad.
If I hadn't run then, we'd both have been caught.
So I ran.{p}

I was safe now...... That's what I thought.
I felt a little sorry for Nakano, but that's survival of the fittest, isn't it?
And in fact, after that I never saw those hands again... I won.{p}

In the room where everyone had fallen silent, Hosoda fumbled his shirt back on.
"Well... that's the end of my story.
Who's going next?"{p}

Luckily, there was a restroom one floor down.
It was free, so we rushed straight in.
......That was a mistake.{p}

Before long, Nakano started moving toward the stalls.
Not that Nakano was moving on his own.
The invisible hands were carrying him toward a stall.{p}

Little by little, Nakano got closer to the stall.
His feet were already almost inside it.
As he got closer to the stall, the hands holding Nakano gradually started to become visible.{p}

Nakano vanished into the stall, leaving only his hands outside.
He was flailing his hands, desperately trying to grab hold of something.
Just like the ghost hands I'd seen at the first restroom...{p}

Of course I went to look.
I didn't want to be so bothered by that restroom that I couldn't focus on the exam.
There were lots of people around, so I figured nothing dangerous would happen.{p}
